    "subtitle": "Complete guide to Equivalence Partitioning and Boundary Value Analysis",
    "ecTitle": "Equivalence Partitioning (EC)",
    "ecDesc": "A black-box method where input data is divided into equivalence classes — sets of values that are processed the same way by the function.",
    "ecPrinciple": "One test from each class is sufficient: if the class works the same for one representative, it will work the same for all.",
    "ecExample1": "For the «Age» field (0–120) there are 3 classes:",
